    {
      "id": "endpoint-anchor-pass-procedure",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Pass Procedure",
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": 330
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 500,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Pass procedure\n\n1. Confirm the named `section-output` edge persists that semantic endpoint.\n2. Confirm an otherwise ordinary node remains connectable through `root`.\n3. Focus **One Port, Two Handles**. Both anchors must represent `result`; dragging either must not create two semantic Ports.\n4. Unfocus **Hidden Handle, Live Port**. Its handle may disappear, but its Port and edge must survive.\n5. Confirm the legacy `right` edge remains readable. Its migration interpretation is `root` with `right` as the visual anchor unless `right` is explicitly exposed semantically.\n6. Focus the edge entering **Edge Reassignment Target**. Move its endpoint from the left anchor to the top anchor: `targetPort` must remain `accept`. Move it to the right anchor: `targetPort` must become `alternate`.\n7. Save, reload, pan, and move nodes. Labels and anchors must remain attached to their handles, and every edge must retain its semantic endpoints.\n\n## Serialized contract\n\n`sourcePort` / `targetPort` identify meaning. `sourceAnchor` / `targetAnchor` identify drawing and interaction placement."
        },
        "renderShape": {
          "kind": "markdown"
        }
      }
    },
